# What NOT to upload to Google Cloud Build.
#
# CRITICAL: without this file, gcloud falls back to .gitignore semantics.
# That mostly works here, but being explicit guarantees the 2.5 GB of sample
# video never gets uploaded to Cloud Build — which would make every deploy
# take an hour and could incur storage charges.
#
# Note: this controls what is UPLOADED to Cloud Build.
# .dockerignore separately controls what goes INTO the image.

# Never upload — 2.5 GB of local footage
Sample Videos for Mobility Assessment/
Sample Videos for Strength Assessment/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.MOV
*.MP4
*.avi
*.mkv

# Dependencies — reinstalled during the image build
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
venv/
.venv/
**/venv/
**/.venv/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Build output — the image builds this fresh
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# Model weights — the Dockerfile downloads these at build time
*.task

# Runtime state
backend/sessions/
backend/temp_uploads/
processor/eval/cache/

# Version control and local tooling
.git/
.github/
.vercel/
.claude/
.cursor/

# Docs and local-only material not needed to build the image
Specification Files/
Mobility Assessment Redesign*/
*.md
!deploy/hf-space/README.md

# Local scratch
sample.js
test_analysis.py
test_local.py
update_exercises.js
update_exercises.py
frontend/@/

# Secrets / OS
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.log
